# -- LHAPDF grid sets --------------------------------------------------------
# The vendored grids are large (NNPDF4.0 ~1.5 GB extracted per suite, JAM ~253 MB)
# and are *inputs*, reproducible by download, so they stay out of git history.
#
# The suites tolerate their absence: config.py's `_read_set_info` looks in the
# extraction root, then the LHAPDF install, then falls back to reading the
# `.info` member straight out of the tarball, and returns `{}` if none is found
# -- callers skip rather than crash.  So a fresh clone without the grids still
# imports; only *generation* needs them.
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
lhapdf/

# -- caches ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fingerprint-validated and rebuilt on demand.  A threaded BLAS reassociates
# contractions inside a single call, so a cache file is not even bitwise
# reproducible across machines -- committing one would be committing noise.
# (17 MB per small suite.)
_kernel_cache/
_inference_cache/
.matplotlib/

# -- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
venv/
.venv/


# ============================================================================
# DELIBERATELY TRACKED, 2026-08-16
# ============================================================================
# `data/`, `results/`, `closure_logs/`, `campaign/` and the figures used to be
# ignored here as "reproducible artifacts".  They are now tracked ON PURPOSE.
#
# Reproducing them is not cheap.  The 144-cell campaign under `campaign/` took
# ~80 minutes at 3 concurrent fits on a 36 GB machine, and regenerating the
# `data/truthQ_*` members needs the 3.5 GB of LHAPDF grids that this file still
# (correctly) excludes.  Without the results committed, a fresh clone cannot
# check a single number in README.md.
#
# The cost stays bounded because the two genuinely large things remain ignored:
# `lhapdf/` (3.5 GB) and `_kernel_cache/` (17 MB per small suite).  What is
# tracked is ~40 MB -- truth curves, DIS systematics, per-run summaries, the
# campaign's 144 JSON rows, and the figures.
#
# Figures are tracked too.  Per each package's CLAUDE.md the plots ARE the
# deliverable here, and a figure that only ever existed in a transcript is a
# result that did not land.
